  "title": "Commit-message gate rules reach the commit scan",
  "summary": "Adds two structural commit-message rules — `commit-subject-full-stop` and `commit-subject-missing` — to the writing lint's commit context, and introduces `COMMIT_GATE_RULES`, the four rules a commit message must pass in a gate. The `commit-msg` hook already ran the writing lint; this change makes the commit scan (`osf scan --commits`, used by the pre-push checkpoint and the pull request check) run the same gate detectors through `commit_gate_findings`, so a bad subject is caught on both paths. Rule metadata gains Coverage sections and `docs/development.md` gains a table of which rules each path enforces.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture"
  ],
